[cot:thought] Global crude steel
[cot:thought] production is roughly 1.89 billion tonnes. China dominates with about 1,019 million tonnes, almost entirely via blast furnace.
[cot:thought] The United States and Turkey rely heavily on electric arc furnaces. Japan and South Korea remain blast furnace heavy. India shows a gradual shift toward electric arc furnaces.
[cot:thought] The United States
